{ ch: 16, title: "The Resurrection", qs: [
{q:"Why did the women buy spices?",o:["For the keeping of the Passover","So that they might go and anoint Jesus","For the service at the temple","For the use of their own household"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:1",e:"The Sabbath had passed."},
{q:"Which three women are named going to the tomb?",o:["Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, and Salome","Mary, Martha of Bethany, and Joanna the wife of Chuza","Mary Magdalene, Susanna, and Elizabeth the mother of John","Salome, Joanna, and Mary the wife of Clopas the elder"],a:0,r:"Mark 16:1",e:"The same group named at the cross, with slight variation."},
{q:"When did the women come to the tomb?",o:["At midnight on the Sabbath, while the guards were still keeping watch","Very early on the first day of the week, when the sun had risen","At noon on the first day, after they had bought the spices in the city","On the Sabbath evening, as soon as the sun had gone down over the hills"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:2",e:"Mark gives an unusually specific time."},
{q:"What were the women asking one another on the way?",o:["“Will the guards at the tomb stop us going in?”","“Who will roll away the stone for us from the entrance?”","“Is it not too early yet, while it is still dark?”","“Should we not wait here for the disciples first?”"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:3",e:"A practical worry."},
{q:"What did the women find when they reached the tomb on the first day of the week?",o:["The stone still sealed, just as it had been left","The stone rolled back, though it was very large","The guards asleep on the ground beside the door","The tomb standing open, with no stone at all there"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:4",e:"Mark notes the size of the stone."},
{q:"Whom did the women see inside the tomb on the first day of the week?",o:["Two men standing by them in dazzling apparel, whose faces shone as light","A young man sitting on the right side, dressed in a white robe","The Lord himself standing where the body had been laid, and they knew him","No one at all, for the tomb was empty and the linen cloths lay folded"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:5",e:"They were alarmed."},
{q:"What did the young man say?",o:["“Do not weep; go quickly and bring Peter and John to this place”","“He has risen; he is not here. See the place where they laid him”","“Why do you seek the living among the dead? Remember what he told you”","“Wait here until he comes, for he will show himself to you first of all”"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:6",e:"He names him “Jesus of Nazareth, who was crucified.”"},
{q:"Which disciple is singled out by name in the message?",o:["John","Peter","James","Andrew"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:7",e:"“Tell his disciples and Peter” — a word of restoration unique to Mark."},
{q:"Where were the disciples told they would see Jesus?",o:["Jerusalem","Galilee","Bethany","On the Mount of Olives"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:7",e:"Just as he had told them."},
{q:"How did the women respond at Mark 16:8?",o:["They rejoiced greatly and ran to bring the news to the eleven at once","They fled, trembling and astonished, and said nothing to anyone, for they were afraid","They went straight to Peter without delay and told him all they had seen","They stayed at the tomb until the evening, waiting for the Lord to appear"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:8",e:"Many of the earliest manuscripts end the Gospel here."},
{q:"What is notable about Mark 16:9-20 in the manuscript tradition?",o:["It is the oldest portion of the whole Gospel of Mark","Many of the earliest manuscripts do not include it","It was written by Peter himself and added afterwards","It appears twice over, in two differing arrangements"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:9-20",e:"Check which ending your quiz uses before drilling this section."},
{q:"To whom did Jesus appear first, according to the longer ending?",o:["Peter","Mary Magdalene","The eleven","Two on the road"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:9",e:"Early on the first day of the week."},
{q:"How many demons had Jesus cast out of Mary Magdalene?",o:["Three","Five","Seven","Twelve"],a:2,r:"Mark 16:9",e:"Mentioned in the longer ending."},
{q:"How did the disciples react to Mary Magdalene's report?",o:["They rejoiced","They would not believe it","They ran to the tomb","They prayed"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:11",e:"They were mourning and weeping."},
{q:"How did Jesus appear to the two walking into the country?",o:["As a gardener","In another form","As a stranger on a boat","As a shepherd"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:12",e:"They too were not believed."},
{q:"What did Jesus rebuke the eleven for?",o:["Their fear of the rulers in the city","Their unbelief and hardness of heart","Their absence from the cross that day","Their arguing over who was greatest"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:14",e:"Because they had not believed those who saw him risen."},
{q:"How is the Great Commission worded in Mark?",o:["“Go therefore and make disciples of all nations, baptising them”","“Go into all the world and proclaim the gospel to the whole creation”","“You shall be my witnesses to the very ends of the earth”","“Feed my lambs, and tend my sheep, and follow after me”"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:15",e:"Mark's distinctive phrasing."},
{q:"“Whoever believes and is baptized will be saved, but whoever does not believe will be ___.”",o:["Lost","Condemned","Judged","Cast out"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:16",e:"From the longer ending."},
{q:"Which sign is NOT listed as accompanying those who believe?",o:["Casting out demons","Speaking in new tongues","Raising the dead","Picking up serpents"],a:2,r:"Mark 16:17-18",e:"The list includes drinking deadly poison unharmed and laying hands on the sick."},
{q:"Where did Jesus sit after he was taken up?",o:["On the Mount of Olives","At the right hand of God","In the temple","Among the angels"],a:1,r:"Mark 16:19",e:"The Gospel closes with the disciples preaching everywhere."}
]}
